  "ok": true,
  "value": {
    "id": "FR-SVL-002",
    "title": "Servlet request mapping: raw path minus context path and servlet mapping, raw query, headers, and the same application types as on the embedded engine",
    "type": "functional",
    "target": "wave-8",
    "status": "verified",
    "scope": "SVL",
    "filePath": "docs/spec/14.servlet-adapter.srs.md",
    "headingLine": 291,
    "metadata": {
      "Type": "functional",
      "Target": "wave-8",
      "Status": "verified",
      "Priority": "high",
      "Tags": "wave-8, feasibility:high, servlet, request, paths",
      "Risk": "high",
      "Stability": "evolving",
      "Verification Method": "test",
      "GitHub Issue": "https://github.com/Snoworca/NaruServe/issues/19",
      "Related Docs": "-"
    },
    "acceptanceCriteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC-1",
        "text": "With context path `/app` and pattern `/api/*`, a request to `/app/api/users/%41;v=1?x=%20` reaches a route `/users/:id` with `req.rawPath()` equal to `/users/%41;v=1`, `req.param(\"id\")` equal to `A;v=1` and `req.query(\"x\")` equal to a space; with pattern `/*` or `/` the same request without `/api` reaches the same route, and a request to the bare servlet root reaches the route `/` (empty remainder is `/`). [D-363; D-399]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 316
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-2",
        "text": "A request whose raw URI does not start with the context path plus the registered prefix at a segment boundary (a test sends `/app/%61pi/users` to pattern `/api/*`) is answered `404` with the standard error body and a request id, and `getServletPath()`, `getPathInfo()` and `getParameter*` are never read, which a recording `HttpServletRequest` proxy asserts. [D-363; r3 W2-004]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 317
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-3",
        "text": "Headers reach `req.header(name)` and `req.headers(name)` with repeated names kept in their per-name order (the Servlet API gives no cross-name order), `Cookie` request headers reach the core cookie parser unchanged (`req.cookie(\"s\")` returns a NaruServe `Cookie`, never `javax.servlet.http.Cookie`), `req.remoteAddress()` is `getRemoteAddr()` and `req.isSecure()` is `isSecure()`; `app.trustProxy(true)` takes effect in the core (FR-ENGINE-008). [D-360]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 318
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-4",
        "text": "A shared case suite — route parameters, query decoding, JSON body and `res.json`, cookies read and written, `404`, `405` with `Allow`, automatic `HEAD` and `OPTIONS`, middleware order, `onError` and the standard error body, `res.file` — runs on the Servlet adapter and on the in-memory adapter with identical statuses and bodies, using the same app definition code, so application code needs no change between engines. [D-360; I-021]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 319
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-5",
        "text": "The path-rejection cases of D-052 (malformed percent-encoding, invalid UTF-8, an encoded `/`, an encoded or raw `NUL`, `.` and `..` segments raw and encoded) sent as raw request lines to the embedded container are answered `400`, or `404` when the container normalises the path and never reaches the servlet, and never `2xx`; the `OPTIONS *` request is sent too, and the observed status of every case is recorded in `docs/api/servlet.md`. [D-052; I-021]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 320
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-6",
        "text": "Header values the framework writes never contain CR or LF on this adapter, and security-related log lines of the adapter carry no token, session id or file content. [I-016; I-017]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 321
      }
    ],
